    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f06e49f_ae21c3a7",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/wifi_chip.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-07T20:55:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consider holding the shared_ptr on the stack. It makes the code slightly simpler. And more importantly, I think that holding the shared_ptr continuously makes more sense semantically.\n\nSaid differently: I don\u0027t think we really want to lock and unlock the HAL in the midst of this method. We don\u0027t, e.g., expect any of the code in here to take a long time.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 198,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "d176d4d8ef0f5aa6b8c8e8732f7f17fab3a54e04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9fd85cb1_aa43af6b",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/wifi_chip.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-10T16:38:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is no longer needed since i\u0027m explicitly using a |is_valid_| boolean to check for the validity.",
      "parentUuid": "5f06e49f_ae21c3a7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 198,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "d176d4d8ef0f5aa6b8c8e8732f7f17fab3a54e04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f06e49f_8eb39f53",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/wifi_chip.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 206,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-07T20:55:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand why this check is needed. Nothing in success path uses legacy_hal_.\n\nIf you simply want to check that this WifiChip is valid, I think the following would be sufficient:\n\n  if (!legacy_hal) {\n    // ...\n  }\n\nAlternatively (still assuming this is just intended to check the validity of this WifiChip), consider adding an explicit is_valid_ boolean field.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 206,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 206,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "d176d4d8ef0f5aa6b8c8e8732f7f17fab3a54e04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f06e49f_8ea4bfb5",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/wifi_chip.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 206,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-07T20:58:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correction: weak_ptr is not convertible to bool. So the code snippet in my previous comment should be replaced with:\n\n  if (legacy_hal_.expired()) {\n    // ...\n  }",
      "parentUuid": "5f06e49f_8eb39f53",
